# Line endings — settled 2026-09-22.
#
# Every blob in this repository is already stored LF. The working tree was CRLF on
# Windows checkouts and LF everywhere else, and that mismatch cost real time five
# times in four days: a 1,512-line `diff -u` of a 17-line change, a file restored
# LF into a CRLF tree, a 4,894-line staging of a 222-line edit, a file that came
# back from an undo with mixed endings, and a `git checkout` that refused to switch
# branches over files nobody had edited.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the working tree LF on every platform, so what git stores and what
# sits on disk are the same bytes and none of the above can recur. This changes no
# file's content — the blobs do not move.
#
# This repository has no .bat, .cmd or .ps1 files. Those are the only ones that
# would need CRLF on disk; add an `eol=crlf` rule here if one is ever introduced.
#
# After pulling this, each person refreshes their working copy ONCE. Commit or
# stash anything in progress first, because the second command discards
# uncommitted changes:
#
#     git rm --cached -r .
#     git reset --hard
#
# Skipping it is harmless — files convert as they are next checked out.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never converted. `text=auto` would detect most of these anyway; they are
# listed so the intent is explicit rather than inferred.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks      binary
